//:: cases TC_PST_11_RequiresConflictsEnsures
//:: tools silicon
//:: verdict Pass

// TC-PST-11: In VerCors, 'x' in an ensures clause refers to the original parameter
// value at the call site (frozen at entry), not a locally-modified copy.
// So requires x == 5; ensures x < 0 would always fail normal verification (5 < 0).
// requires false makes normal verification vacuous, isolating the postSat check:
// ensures x < 0 is satisfiable on its own (e.g., x = -1), so the postSat checker
// must NOT fire.
//
// Under the old combined check (requires ∧ ensures), false ∧ (x < 0) is
// unsatisfiable regardless of the postcondition, so it would have incorrectly
// fired postUnsatisfiable even though the postcondition is independently satisfiable.
requires x > 0;
ensures \result < 0;
void f(int x) { }
